<title>UK: UK notes in circulation rise 6.9 percent.</title>
<headline>UK notes in circulation rise 6.9 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>British bank notes in circulation rose an adjusted 6.9 percent in the week to January 22 over the equivalent year-ago week, the Bank of England said.</p>
<p>Last week the annual adjusted rise was 7.2 percent.</p>
<p>NOTES IN CIRCULATION (in rounded bln stg) -</p>
<p>				Latest week    pvs week     yr-ago week</p>
<p>Notes in circulation     20.589	  20.795	   19.269</p>
<p>Bankers' deposits	   1.990	   2.084	    1.82</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7708</p>
